sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "If the ultimate rule for the universe is simple, it cannot realistically be found by engineering it from observed features; the only practical method is to choose a straightforward representation and systematically search through large numbers of candidate rules.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The fundamental rule cannot be found by working backwards from known laws";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Ultimate Models for the Universe” (from p. 465), p. 468. Scope: methodology for finding a fundamental theory of physics"
}
